# CivicWorkDesk — what does NOT belong in a public Git history.
#
# Two rules decide every line below.
#
#   1. Source, tests, deployment scripts, documentation and provenance (checksums, manifests) are
#      tracked. They are what a reviewer needs and what makes the repository reproducible.
#   2. Generated output, machine-local state, and anything that could carry real data or a secret is
#      not tracked — and a distributable archive is published as a GitHub Release rather than
#      accumulating in normal Git history as an opaque blob.
#
# A note on what this file cannot do: ignoring a path has no effect on history. Anything already
# committed stays reachable until history is rewritten. The publication audit therefore scans every
# blob reachable from every ref, not just the working tree.

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output. The built application reaches Git only inside a staged release payload under
# release/, where it is the reviewable record of what was actually delivered.
dist/
dist-ssr/
dev-dist/
*.local

# Test / tooling output
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/
blob-report/
.playwright/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Environment — never commit a real .env
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor / OS.
# .vscode/settings.json and .vscode/extensions.json ARE tracked on purpose: they are shared project
# configuration, and settings.json is what hides _private_reference/ from the editor's explorer and
# search. Everything else under .vscode is machine-local.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
.vs/
*.code-workspace
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~

# Local logs and scratch output. Deployment logs live under the user's XDG/LOCALAPPDATA state
# directory on the target machine, never in the repository.
*.log
*.tmp
tmp/
.scratch/

# Confidential legacy source material.
# Only the explanatory README is tracked; the original prototype embeds roughly 180 real work records
# — personal names, phone numbers, named organisations — and must never enter Git history.
_private_reference/*
!_private_reference/README.md

# Generated review packages (large binaries; regenerate with npm run review:package).
_review_packages/*
!_review_packages/.gitkeep

# UOS release artefacts.
#
# The delivery archive itself is NOT tracked: it is a build product, and the published copy belongs in
# a GitHub Release where it can be downloaded and checksum-verified. What IS tracked is the staged
# payload, the VERSION metadata and the `.sha256` sidecars — the provenance a reviewer needs to check a
# downloaded archive against, without having to trust the download.
release/*/.runtime/
release/*.tar.gz

# Windows release build output. The installer, the staged payload and the Go build directory are all
# build products: the tracked sources plus the `.sha256` sidecar are the provenance, and the installer
# itself belongs in a GitHub Release where it can be downloaded and checksum-verified. The acceptance
# reports are tracked deliberately -- they are the record of what was measured.
release/windows/.build/
release/windows/civic-work-desk-windows-x64-*/
release/windows/*.exe
release/windows/*.log

# The acceptance reports carry the operator's account name and machine paths, so they follow the same rule
# as tester-collected probe output: reviewed and transcribed into docs/ deliberately, never committed raw.
# Their measured results are in docs/phase-4-windows-rc1.md.
release/windows/acceptance-rc1-*.txt

# The tester instructions beside the installer are a build-derived copy of
# deploy/windows/installer/README-测试说明.txt. Tracking both copies is how they drift apart; the source is
# tracked and the build re-derives this one.
release/windows/README-测试说明.txt

# Distribution archives built by scripts/windows/build-probe-bundle.mjs. Same reasoning as the .tar.gz
# above: the archive is a build product, deterministic from its inputs, so the tracked probe sources plus
# the `.sha256` sidecar are the provenance. The sidecar IS tracked — it is how a tester checks the copy
# they received against what this repository says it should be.
release/*.zip

# Phase-4 Windows probe and acceptance output collected from a tester's machine. These carry host
# names, user profile paths and installed-software inventories; they are reviewed and transcribed into
# docs/ deliberately, never committed raw.
deploy/windows/probe/out/
civic-work-desk-windows-probe-*.txt
civic-work-desk-windows-results-*.txt
